Recommends: tsunyx-launcher (>= 1.7.1), uzunyx-lockkeys (>= 0.3.0), firefox-esr | firefox
Description: Uzunyx global themes for Plasma (Akane and Sora)
 Two dark Plasma look-and-feel packages, "Uzunyx Akane" (the default,
 crimson) and "Uzunyx Sora" (cyan). They share the Uzunyx rounded window
 decoration and window buttons, the Uzunyx Plasma theme (Unity-style task
 manager indicators) and the Kora icon theme (through the "uzunyx" icon
 theme from uzunyx-buttons), and differ in their color scheme
 (uzunyx-colors), wallpaper and the Uzunyx logo on the launcher button. Its desktop layout has a floating, centered
 bottom panel sized to its content, with Tsunyx Launcher as the app menu
 (Kickoff if tsunyx-launcher is not installed) followed by the Tsunyx Search
 box, a task manager that shows window thumbnails when a group of
 windows is clicked, and the Caps Lock / Num Lock indicator from
 uzunyx-lockkeys before the system tray.
 .
 It is set as the system default global theme in /etc/xdg/kdeglobals, so
 new users get it on their first login. Users who already chose a global
 theme keep theirs until they select Uzunyx Akane or Uzunyx Sora in System
 Settings > Colors & Themes > Global Theme.
 .
 Dolphin gets an "Up" button after "Forward" in its main toolbar.
 .
 A plasma-workspace env script makes Plasma rewrite the theme defaults of
 users already on Uzunyx when this package is updated (Plasma only does
 it when the global theme's name changes).
